Id: netw042f
Severity: FAIL
Category: network
Check: check_ntp
Fix: Add server (or pool) lines and restart ntpd.
References: ntp.conf(5)
Controls: CIS 8.4; NIST AU-8, SC-45; ISO 8.17

The NTP daemon is running but its configuration names no remote time
server, so the clock is never corrected. A drifting clock breaks log
correlation, Kerberos, DNSSEC and certificate checks. Add at least one
"server" line pointing at a trustworthy source, for example the
distribution's NTP pool, and restart the daemon.
